# ROM manifest of Ms. Pac-Man on the Pac-Man board. The format is described in the head of
# pacman.manifest.
#
# The file is pacman.rom's layout plus the second program bank at the end, so pacman.rom and
# puckman.rom are a prefix of it and keep their layout and digests. build.tcl writes the
# loader's section table from this manifest and takes those two sizes as its second size
# (ROM_TOTAL_SHORT). This is why the bank comes last here, not in MAME's chip order.
#
# The bank is the core's 0x4000..0x7FFF of the download (CPU 0x8000..0xBFFF), laid out as
# MiSTer's Ms. Pac-Man.mra does: u5 twice, u6, u7 twice. The core decrypts at run time from
# the places MAME's ROM_LOAD names, u5 at 0x8000, u6 at 0x9000, u7 at 0xB000. The core sees a
# loaded bank as Ms. Pac-Man (mod_ms), see game_core.sv.

set     mspacman
title   Ms. Pac-Man (Midway)
zip     mspacman.zip
total   41760
board   2
mirror  6272

section program     0x0000 16384
chip    pacman.6e   4096 e87e059c5be45753f7e9f33dff851f16d6751181
chip    pacman.6f   4096 674d3a7f00d8be5e38b1fdc208ebef5a92d38329
